# Data conversion between gigabyte and kilobyte

Verifies direct data conversion between gigabyte and kilobyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1GB to 1000000KB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5GB yields 1500000.0KB; backward, converting 1KB to 0.0000GB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5KB yields 0.0000GB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1GB
print(forward_whole->to(KB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GB
print(forward_fractional->to(KB))
backward_whole: int = 1KB
print(backward_whole->to(GB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KB
print(backward_fractional->to(GB))

<<< stdout
1000000KB
1500000.0KB
0.0000GB
0.0000GB

<<< stderr
